@page "/blocks/blog"
@using Stil.Docs.Examples.Blocks

<DocsHeader Title="Blog" Eyebrow="Website">
    <Lead>A list of posts with paging, and the layout of an article with a table of contents.</Lead>
</DocsHeader>

<p>
    Like the other <a href="blocks/sections">page blocks</a>, these need <code>&lt;StilHead Blocks /&gt;</code> and
    <code>@@using Stil.Blazor.Blocks</code>. Where the posts come from is up to you: a database, files, or Markdown
    rendered with <a href="components/markdown">StilMarkdown</a> in the article's body.
</p>

<h2 id="posts">Post list</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(Posts)">
    <p>
        <code>StilPostList</code> fits as many <code>StilPostCard</code> columns as there is room for. A card has a
        picture (decorative by default, since the title follows), tags, the title, an excerpt and who wrote it when.
        The title is the card's link and covers the whole card, and tags that are links stay clickable above it.
        <code>Featured</code> spans the list with the picture beside the text. The date is shown in the current
        culture (<code>DateFormat</code>, "d MMMM yyyy" by default) in a <code>time</code> element. Page with a
        <a href="components/navigation#pagination">StilPagination</a> of links (<code>HrefTemplate</code>).
    </p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="article">Article</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(Article)">
    <p>
        <code>StilArticle</code> has a header (an eyebrow that can link back to the blog, the title, a lead and
        <code>StilPostMeta</code>), a picture with a caption, the body in <code>stil-prose</code> with larger reading
        type, and a footer with the tags. <code>Contents</code> lists the headings (with <code>Href</code>
        <code>#id</code>): beside the text on a wide article, where it stays in view, and above it on a narrow one.
        Its title, "On this page", is translated. In a page, the title is the <code>h1</code>; here it is an
        <code>h3</code> (<code>HeadingLevel</code>), under this page's headings.
    </p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<ApiTable Type="typeof(StilPostCard)" />
<ApiTable Type="typeof(StilPostMeta)" />
